  "lineage": "Urdu-language guitar-and-synth pop that began with Nazia and Zoheb Hassan's Biddu-produced Disco Deewane (1980) and was codified by Vital Signs' Dil Dil Pakistan (1987) and Junoon's Sufi rock of the 1990s, recorded at EMI Pakistan Karachi and Lahore: 100-130 BPM backbeat kits, chorused clean guitar and Juno-class pads, tabla or dholak doubling the snare, and Urdu vocals that sit between ghazal phrasing and Western pop melody.",
